00:14:08.890 --> 00:14:13.890
We put it in, Lily has her own
bathroom, and it's in there.

00:14:14.890 --> 00:14:16.840
But getting used to that
space, getting acclimated.

00:14:16.840 --> 00:14:18.100
- And Jade will immediately
know that there's

00:14:18.100 --> 00:14:20.750
a cat present in the
house, via the smell alone.

00:14:20.750 --> 00:14:23.030
- So, a dog can smell, man.

00:14:23.030 --> 00:14:23.980
- Yeah.

00:14:23.980 --> 00:14:26.090
- And especially when there's
a big crack under the door,

00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:28.940
you can see, like, a paw
coming out sometimes.

00:14:28.940 --> 00:14:30.640
She definitely knew something was up.

00:14:30.640 --> 00:14:32.900
But she would sit out
there and kind of whimper,

00:14:32.900 --> 00:14:34.280
and sniff, and sniff, and sniff.

00:14:34.280 --> 00:14:39.280
But, after a few days of
that, stage two was put Sokka

00:14:39.480 --> 00:14:41.590
in her, his carrier.

00:14:41.590 --> 00:14:44.850
That's the other thing,
is calling Sokka her

00:14:44.850 --> 00:14:46.050
for the longest time.

00:14:46.050 --> 00:14:46.890
- I did that.

00:14:46.890 --> 00:14:49.480
- Because Jade, you're so
used to having one animal

00:14:49.480 --> 00:14:51.070
in the house that's a her,

00:14:51.070 --> 00:14:53.680
you're not used to a he in the house.

00:14:53.680 --> 00:14:55.960
You put him in the little crate,

00:14:55.960 --> 00:14:57.960
and then you let Jade come in,

00:14:57.960 --> 00:14:59.790
and he's protected in the crate,

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:03.163
and then Jade can
inspect the cat visually,

00:15:04.560 --> 00:15:07.265
nasally, but not actually devour.

00:15:07.265 --> 00:15:10.220
- And how did that go the first time.

00:15:10.220 --> 00:15:13.650
- Jade was really keyed
up, and Sokka just seemed,

00:15:13.650 --> 00:15:18.173
like, not too afraid, just kind of like.

00:15:19.070 --> 00:15:21.630
I mean, at first, there
was some nose touching.

00:15:21.630 --> 00:15:24.461
But then there was, and some cringing,

00:15:24.461 --> 00:15:28.210
but then it was mostly
just, the kitten, like,

00:15:28.210 --> 00:15:30.580
didn't care that much.

00:15:30.580 --> 00:15:31.960
It's, like, very much convinced

00:15:31.960 --> 00:15:34.310
that Jade could not get
to him, which was true.

00:15:35.860 --> 00:15:40.860
So there were a number of
days of bringing in the dog

00:15:41.030 --> 00:15:45.090
to sniff the crate and the
cat in full protection.

00:15:45.090 --> 00:15:49.333
But then I'm like, the next
stage is to get the cat out.

00:15:50.563 --> 00:15:52.044
- Put it in a dog costume.

00:15:52.044 --> 00:15:53.620
(link laughs)

00:15:53.620 --> 00:15:55.710
There's multiple steps to this.

00:15:55.710 --> 00:15:59.190
- And then just let them meet each other.

00:15:59.190 --> 00:16:02.220
So what I ended up doing was,

00:16:02.220 --> 00:16:04.030
and at this point I kinda
got scared for Jade.

00:16:04.030 --> 00:16:08.460
I was like, I think that, I
mean, the claws on this animal.

00:16:08.460 --> 00:16:09.360
- Cat's can hurt a dog.

00:16:09.360 --> 00:16:13.047
- Like, could blind my dog.

00:16:13.047 --> 00:16:15.618
That would be very upsetting to me.

00:16:15.618 --> 00:16:16.608
- Yeah.

00:16:16.608 --> 00:16:19.340
- If a Jade eyeball got scratched out

00:16:20.400 --> 00:16:22.580
because of, like, how
I'm going about this.

00:16:22.580 --> 00:16:24.320
So I would hold Jade in my lap.

00:16:24.320 --> 00:16:28.160
I would restrain Jade, and
then we would let the cat

00:16:28.160 --> 00:16:31.580
out of the crate, and just
kind of run around the room.

00:16:34.740 --> 00:16:39.590
After a few days of this,
eventually it was like letting

00:16:39.590 --> 00:16:41.380
them run around a little bit.

00:16:41.380 --> 00:16:44.530
Jade would chase the
cat underneath the bed.

00:16:44.530 --> 00:16:46.540
But Jade was afraid to
go underneath the bed,

00:16:46.540 --> 00:16:49.537
even though she should
totally be able to do that.

00:16:49.537 --> 00:16:52.820
- But she wasn't mad,
she was playing with her.

00:16:52.820 --> 00:16:56.659
- She was very inquisitive,
yeah, her tail was wagging.

00:16:56.659 --> 00:16:57.770
- Like, she was afraid to
go under the bed, period,

00:16:57.770 --> 00:16:58.640
or she was afraid to go under the bed

00:16:58.640 --> 00:16:59.830
when the cat's under there?

00:16:59.830 --> 00:17:01.149
- I think period.

00:17:01.149 --> 00:17:02.236
(both laughing)

00:17:02.236 --> 00:17:06.217
Yeah, she's got her own.

00:17:06.217 --> 00:17:07.780
- She's got some issues.

00:17:07.780 --> 00:17:08.613
- Issues.

00:17:08.613 --> 00:17:09.520
- Yeah.

00:17:09.520 --> 00:17:12.790
But the cat would, I mean,
the cat could not just,

00:17:12.790 --> 00:17:13.930
wouldn't go in and just cower.

00:17:13.930 --> 00:17:15.420
The cat would keep coming back out

00:17:15.420 --> 00:17:17.987
and, like, giving Jade a
little taste of catness,

00:17:17.987 --> 00:17:19.202
and then going back in.

00:17:19.202 --> 00:17:20.240
- What about, like, the pat, the pity pats

00:17:20.240 --> 00:17:22.510
that the cat would do with the hand?

00:17:22.510 --> 00:17:24.554
They're really good at
that, did he do that?

00:17:24.554 --> 00:17:26.600
- That eventually started happening,

00:17:26.600 --> 00:17:29.290
like a little batting of the face.

00:17:29.290 --> 00:17:30.660
- That's my favorite thing about cats.

00:17:30.660 --> 00:17:34.250
- A lot of that, like, bowing
up and doing the cat pose,

00:17:34.250 --> 00:17:36.767
where it's like, the fur
goes up and the back goes up.

00:17:36.767 --> 00:17:39.607
You know those, like
the Halloween cat pose?

00:17:39.607 --> 00:17:43.510
Or I guess you just call
that the Cat in yoga.

00:17:43.510 --> 00:17:45.281
- Mm, Cat and Cow, yeah.

00:17:45.281 --> 00:17:47.280
- No Cow, just the Cat.

00:17:47.280 --> 00:17:48.113
- Yeah, just the Cat.

00:17:48.113 --> 00:17:50.400
- So, over a few weeks
we got them to the point

00:17:50.400 --> 00:17:52.630
that they could be in
the same room together.

00:17:52.630 --> 00:17:55.870
And they just, they would,
Jade would start coming out,

00:17:55.870 --> 00:17:58.370
and then he would start
coming out of the room

00:17:58.370 --> 00:18:00.210
and seeing the rest of the house.

00:18:00.210 --> 00:18:04.640
And Jade would chase the
cat back into the room.

00:18:04.640 --> 00:18:06.090
And then Jade would be happy.

00:18:07.010 --> 00:18:10.013
And then after a while,
Sokka would run out,

00:18:10.013 --> 00:18:12.310
and Jade would chase the cat.

00:18:12.310 --> 00:18:15.600
And then the cat would run away.

00:18:15.600 --> 00:18:19.080
And then the cat would come
back, and Jade would run.

00:18:19.080 --> 00:18:20.360
And then it got to a point
where they were, like,

00:18:20.360 --> 00:18:21.900
chasing each other all
around the living room.

00:18:21.900 --> 00:18:23.610
- But this is still playful.

00:18:23.610 --> 00:18:24.653
And it's, well,

00:18:25.720 --> 00:18:30.020
I think Jade saw it as playful

00:18:30.020 --> 00:18:35.020
and I think Sokka saw it as
military training or something.

00:18:36.360 --> 00:18:38.105
You know, it was like, "I'm gonna engage."

00:18:38.105 --> 00:18:41.568
And everything seems like
training for this cat.

00:18:41.568 --> 00:18:43.197
- How do you know that?

00:18:43.197 --> 00:18:46.010
- 'Cause he is a wild beast.

00:18:46.010 --> 00:18:51.010
I mean, every point of
observation, for me,

00:18:51.570 --> 00:18:54.730
supports the fact that this
thing is not tame in any way.

00:18:54.730 --> 00:18:58.480
I mean, his pupils
dilate, and they're just,

00:18:58.480 --> 00:19:00.840
like, totally black.

00:19:00.840 --> 00:19:04.700
Like, it reminds me of the cat in "Shrek."

00:19:04.700 --> 00:19:07.410
Remember when he was, like,
his pupils would just dilate,

00:19:07.410 --> 00:19:08.480
and he'd go into this.

00:19:08.480 --> 00:19:09.470
- That makes him cute, though.

00:19:09.470 --> 00:19:12.470
- Oh, no, when he would
do it, it would be like

00:19:12.470 --> 00:19:15.540
he entered some fugue state
where he stalks around

00:19:15.540 --> 00:19:19.740
the house, and just looking
for the next thing to attack.

00:19:19.740 --> 00:19:24.130
I mean, he'll shred the edge
of the couch with his claws.

00:19:24.130 --> 00:19:28.750
- But they are less, I
mean, I have to believe

00:19:28.750 --> 00:19:33.010
that a cat, a current cat, is much closer

00:19:33.010 --> 00:19:35.920
to the original of whatever
was taken from the wild

00:19:35.920 --> 00:19:37.990
to be domesticated than a dog is.

00:19:37.990 --> 00:19:40.390
- I was talking to Lily
about this last night.

00:19:40.390 --> 00:19:41.490
- It's gotta be wildly different.

00:19:41.490 --> 00:19:45.410
- I was like, "When I
look at this cat, Lily,

00:19:45.410 --> 00:19:49.630
it's like, I can see a tiger in this cat."

00:19:49.630 --> 00:19:52.180
- I don't think they
come from tigers though.

00:19:52.180 --> 00:19:54.060
- A huge, ferocious tiger.

00:19:54.060 --> 00:19:57.280
But when I look at a dog,
the only thing I can see

00:19:57.280 --> 00:20:00.820
is a reasonably sized wolf.

00:20:00.820 --> 00:20:04.470
You know, it's like, it has the same form

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:06.383
as something that could just,

00:20:07.928 --> 00:20:12.928
it's like a zoological tank,
that's what a tiger is, man.

00:20:13.150 --> 00:20:14.090
It's a furry tank.

00:20:14.090 --> 00:20:16.980
- But, what I'm saying
is I think that a cat,

00:20:16.980 --> 00:20:20.100
I think, like, a house cat is,

00:20:20.100 --> 00:20:24.893
if you go back 15,000
years, 10,000, 20,000 years,

00:20:25.940 --> 00:20:28.500
whatever, there'd be like,

00:20:28.500 --> 00:20:31.500
cats that look like your
cat just out in the wild.

00:20:31.500 --> 00:20:33.560
Think about a bobcat, right.

00:20:33.560 --> 00:20:38.320
A bobcat is not that
different than a cat, right?

00:20:38.320 --> 00:20:43.320
But Jade and Barbara look
absolutely nothing like a wolf.

00:20:44.019 --> 00:20:45.510
That's what I was saying.

00:20:45.510 --> 00:20:48.010
Is that the difference
between what was domesticated

00:20:48.010 --> 00:20:51.420
and what we have is so different in a dog.

00:20:51.420 --> 00:20:54.020
But there hasn't been nearly as much,

00:20:54.020 --> 00:20:58.150
there's also not nearly as
much variety genetically.

00:20:58.150 --> 00:20:59.610
I mean, I know there's
like the Maine Coon,

00:20:59.610 --> 00:21:01.060
which is like this giant cat.

00:21:01.060 --> 00:21:01.991
- Huge, right.

00:21:01.991 --> 00:21:02.824
- But just think about
the difference between

00:21:02.824 --> 00:21:07.370
a Teacup Poodle, Chihuahua,
and a Great Dane.

00:21:07.370 --> 00:21:09.220
They're the same species, man.

00:21:09.220 --> 00:21:11.740
But they don't have that kind
of genetic variety in a cat.

00:21:11.740 --> 00:21:14.930
And is that just because we
haven't chosen to breed them

00:21:14.930 --> 00:21:15.763
in the same way?

00:21:15.763 --> 00:21:18.320
I think all it means
is that they're closer

00:21:18.320 --> 00:21:19.995
to the original, wild thing, for sure.

00:21:19.995 --> 00:21:21.250
- Maybe they're not as malleable.

00:21:21.250 --> 00:21:23.940
- And that's why they can just
go live in the wild, feral.

00:21:23.940 --> 00:21:27.300
If you put Barbara, I mean,
when we put Barbara outside

00:21:27.300 --> 00:21:30.840
to pee in our fenced in
backyard, which, by the way,

00:21:30.840 --> 00:21:33.617
doesn't even have real
grass, Jessie's like,

00:21:33.617 --> 00:21:34.647
"You gotta keep an eye on her."

00:21:34.647 --> 00:21:36.160
- Oh, and you do have to.

00:21:36.160 --> 00:21:36.993
- Because-

00:21:36.993 --> 00:21:37.826
- A coyote will come.

00:21:37.826 --> 00:21:40.040
- A coyote, a, you know,
mountain lion, whatever.

00:21:40.040 --> 00:21:42.350
- I think a coyote would get a cat, too.

00:21:42.350 --> 00:21:44.752
But they'll put up a much better fight.

00:21:44.752 --> 00:21:46.663
- The cat has a better chance to get away.

00:21:46.663 --> 00:21:47.496
- A better fighting chance.

00:21:47.496 --> 00:21:48.470
- Barbara is like a marshmallow

00:21:48.470 --> 00:21:51.070
that just rolls directly
into the coyote's mouth.

00:21:51.070 --> 00:21:52.840
- One of the biggest
adjustments we had to make

00:21:52.840 --> 00:21:54.720
was remembering to
close the door behind us

00:21:54.720 --> 00:21:56.530
when we let Jade out.

00:21:56.530 --> 00:21:59.400
'Cause we escort Jade
out to watch for coyotes.

00:21:59.400 --> 00:22:00.620
- 'Cause the cat is your prisoner.

00:22:00.620 --> 00:22:02.194
- The cat is the prisoner, yes.

00:22:02.194 --> 00:22:05.884
I mean, if the cat got
out, the cat got out once,

00:22:05.884 --> 00:22:09.730
and immediately darted out the door,

00:22:09.730 --> 00:22:12.970
went to the right, and
then went through a hole,

00:22:12.970 --> 00:22:14.620
and went under the house.

00:22:14.620 --> 00:22:15.700
Just like that.

00:22:15.700 --> 00:22:17.650
The only time that Sokka's
been out of the house,

00:22:17.650 --> 00:22:20.670
it went under the house immediately.

00:22:20.670 --> 00:22:21.847
And, I mean.

00:22:21.847 --> 00:22:23.108
- Now how did you solve that?

00:22:23.108 --> 00:22:25.960
- Lily brought out some tinkly thing

00:22:25.960 --> 00:22:28.657
that it was enticed to attack.

00:22:28.657 --> 00:22:30.060
And that's what you do.

00:22:30.060 --> 00:22:34.400
I mean, it sees feet
as, like, moving meat.

00:22:34.400 --> 00:22:39.281
If you're barefoot, this thing will attack

00:22:39.281 --> 00:22:42.980
and decimate your toes,
your heel, everything.

00:22:42.980 --> 00:22:45.630
The cat likes to bite everything.

00:22:45.630 --> 00:22:48.828
It's just like, it's like a killer saying,

00:22:48.828 --> 00:22:53.380
"I choked him just to see what
it felt like to kill a man."

00:22:53.380 --> 00:22:54.260
You know?

00:22:54.260 --> 00:22:55.943
- You're putting a lot onto this cat.

00:22:55.943 --> 00:22:58.457
- He sinks his teeth into-

00:22:58.457 --> 00:22:59.570
- You think the cat would eat your foot

00:22:59.570 --> 00:23:00.420
if you didn't move it?

00:23:00.420 --> 00:23:01.270
- Hell, yes.

00:23:01.270 --> 00:23:02.850
- He would keep eating it?

00:23:02.850 --> 00:23:05.870
- Well, he doesn't eat
it, he likes the feeling

00:23:05.870 --> 00:23:10.850
of his razor sharp teeth
slowly sinking into it.

